* use "vars_term_impl" (and same for funs/funas/roots/funas_args and rule/trs)
  instead of "vars_term_list in "implementations" (i.e., for code generation).
  The former is supposed to provide a reasonably efficient implementation for
  set-based abstract functions, while the latter is used when order and
  multiplicity are wanted. Gradually replace "_list" by "_impl", when intended.
* gradually get rid of "+#+" and "+@+". The former is "shows x o y" the latter
  "x o y", which is easier to read and more familiar to the average user.
* gradually try to avoid references to _Impl theories in non _Impl theories.
  Move definitions and facts if necessary.
* dissolve Decomp and SubList into other theories
* merge RPO_Impl with RPO_Memoized
* think about whether Positions should become [nat]
* gradually improve "interface" and docu (to facilitate 3rd party contributions)
* gradually get rid of TODOs (cf. output of ./todos.sh)
* improve uncurrying (strategy, relative rules with top-uncurrying)
* improve techniques where weak rules are silently treated as strict rules:
  - Matchbounds
* Replace lemmas about sharp/plain/unsharp/clean by general lemmas about
  map_term, map_subst, ...
* define sharp/plain/unsharp/clean via map functions.
